# Snapshot fixtures are compared byte-for-byte against source-generator output, so their line
# endings have to match whatever the generator that produced them emits.
#
# For Uno's own generators that is the host's newline: they build their output with
# StringBuilder.AppendLine, i.e. Environment.NewLine. The repository-wide `* text=auto` is exactly
# right for those -- it stores LF and materializes the host's newline on checkout, so the fixture
# follows the generator on every platform. They are deliberately left to inherit it.
#
# It is wrong for the files below, whose newlines do NOT follow the host, so a converted checkout
# would move them away from the output they are compared against.
#
# ObservablePropertyGenerator_*: produced by a generator shipped as a NuGet package, which baked the
# newlines of its own sources at package build time and therefore emits CRLF on every host.
# Normalized, they only ever matched on a checkout that happened to restore CRLF -- and git hid it:
# the working copy kept its CRLF bytes while the blob held LF, and `git status` reported no change
# because the clean filter normalized them back on comparison.
#
# *.codebehind.g.cs: built from a verbatim string literal rather than AppendLine, so its newlines
# would be those of the emitter's own source file as checked out. XamlCodeBehindEmitter pins them to
# LF instead, which is what these have to keep.
ObservablePropertyGenerator_*.g.cs -text
*.codebehind.g.cs -text
